  "question": {
    "text": "The slope of the tangent to the curve $x=3 t^2+1$, $y=t^3-1$ at $x=1$ is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zqzMj",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rhEYn",
      "text": "<br />0",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PaV5X",
      "text": "<br />-2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Cdcr9",
      "text": "$\\infty$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given curve is $x=3 t^2+1$<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/i96DNHHTo_FW52n7W2lHdlYYGcu7QfMaYWl6ffqxwB0.original.fullsize.png\"><br><br />Second curve is $y=t^3-1$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/Amt76KEG_dlbSyhjkiFOkKWDMGfdWOuylzm_d0Px6vA.original.fullsize.png\"><br><br />$\\therefore \\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{d y}{d t} \\times \\frac{d t}{d x}=3 t^2 \\times \\frac{1}{6 t}=\\frac{t}{2}$<br />But from (i) when $x=1$<br />we have $1=3 t^2+1 \\Rightarrow 3 t^2=0 \\Rightarrow t=0$<br />$\\therefore$ When $\\mathrm{x}=1$ then $\\mathrm{t}=0 \\quad \\therefore \\frac{\\mathrm{dy}}{\\mathrm{dx}}=\\mathbf{0}$<br />Hence, slope of the tangent to the curve $=0$",
    "image": null
  },
